  "_doc": "AGENT VIEW (Phase 052): the one limited interface. BigvilleGame.agent_view(actor) and GET /api/view return only what the resident could perceive and know, built by domains/agent_view.py from the whitelist below. AGENT_VIEW_WHITELIST names the keys each section may carry; the builder raises on any other key, and domains/agent_view_check.py checks the whitelist itself. AGENT_VIEW_REFEREE_ONLY names engine fields that must never appear in an agent view (the leak test checks every key and every string). AGENT_VIEW_QUANTITIES maps each view field that carries a number in words to its lexicon table (domains/lexicon.py), so a field with no words cannot be published. MAP_GLYPHS draws the map patch (terrain only, no occupants, no coordinates): a glyph and its words for each terrain name in TERRAIN_MOVEMENT, plus 'unknown' for off-map ground and 'player' for the resident's own cell. VIEW_WORDS, PRECISION_WORDS and ACTION_WORDS are the fixed phrases of the view (a person's words, not the engine's). Every phrase has no digit: a digit in a view string is a raw number. KNOWS_LIMIT caps the 'knows' list (APPROX: a display cap, not a world fact). The glyphs and the cap are model choices and are marked APPROX. Phase 053 replaces the map patch with the fogged map.",
